1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,133
By 2048, 124 trillion dollars of U.S. wealth will change hands.

2
00:00:06,733 --> 00:00:13,200
And 55 percent of spouses and heirs say they won't, or didn't, keep their benefactor's advisor.

3
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:25,783
A business sale doesn't just move money. It moves a family. In five interviews, owners told us: letting go is personal, family members need clearer roles, and knowledge needs a handover.

4
00:00:26,383 --> 00:00:34,650
Meet Margaret Wilson, selling the company she built, and Alex Lee, her PNC advisor. One sale, two sides.

5
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:43,517
Family Table is a consent-based AI coordination layer that guides them through three steps: Align, Allocate, Activate.

6
00:00:44,117 --> 00:00:52,184
First, Align. Claire checks in privately. AI turns her words into themes, and she chooses what Alex sees.

7
00:00:52,784 --> 00:01:03,101
Alex sees themes, not words. Margaret thought the kids agreed. The widest gap is fairness. AI prepares the analysis; Alex makes the call.

8
00:01:03,701 --> 00:01:12,601
Then, Allocate. Sam sees his own number under every split, votes in private, and three choices turn twelve plans into one.

9
00:01:13,201 --> 00:01:21,101
Then, Activate. Sam asks a person, not a bot. AI drafts the reply; Alex checks it and sends it.

10
00:01:21,701 --> 00:01:27,101
Nothing reaches the family until the advisor approves it, and every output is logged.

11
00:01:27,701 --> 00:01:39,618
Why only PNC? Three proprietary assets in one consented stack: relationship signals the advisor reviews, private-by-default family intelligence, and a household graph.

12
00:01:40,218 --> 00:01:50,935
PNC administers 499 billion dollars in client assets. We validate for six weeks, then pilot for 90 days with ten families and three advisors.

13
00:01:51,535 --> 00:01:56,435
Family Table. Crafting the family future, today.
